+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry validates tool calls against the JSON Schema supplied by the resolved tool definition before executing them.
+
+- Missing required fields, wrong types and enum violations return a descriptive tool result without invoking the executor or exposing input values ([validated by: rejects missing and invalid fields without invoking the executor or exposing values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- Valid input, including unlisted extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged exactly once, without applying defaults or coercion ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L36)).
+- An uncompilable static schema fails at registration with an error naming the tool ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration with the tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L51)).
+- A function-valued definition is validated against the schema resolved for the current call ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition against its current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L58)).
diff --git a/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts b/src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts
